{"ts":"2026-05-12T19:03:42Z","session":"65fbc6a6-f398-4cd4-b478-4d013cd76c21","event":"prompt","text":"Add 4 AI features to the React frontend of the Macys Marketing GUI. The Render backend exposes 4 endpoints at https://macys-api-n6f3.onrender.com that we will call. All 4 features use real AI through TritonAI.\n\nCRITICAL RULES (NON NEGOTIABLE):\n- Never use em dashes or any dashes anywhere in code, comments, JSX, copy, or commit messages. Use commas, periods, parentheses, or rewording.\n- Git author: merna, email msaad@ucsd.edu. No co author lines.\n- Push to BOTH origin and personal remotes at the end.\n- Do NOT break the existing M2 approval flow. ADD components, do not REPLACE.\n- All AI generated text gets a small \"AI\" badge or icon to make AI involvement clear.\n- Loading states are subtle, not flashy. Skeleton rows or a small spinner.\n- Error states are graceful: if the API fails, show \"AI temporarily unavailable\" and let the user proceed manually.\n- Match the existing Tailwind color scheme. No new colors, no new design tokens.\n\nCONTEXT:\n- Frontend lives at gui/ inside this repo\n- It is a Next.js app using app router and Tailwind CSS\n- Existing approval flow has personas (Sarah, VP, Diego, Anna), a campaign sidebar, approval buttons\n- API base URL: https://macys-api-n6f3.onrender.com\n- The first AI call after the server is idle takes 30 to 60 seconds (lazy model load); subsequent calls take 13 to 20 seconds\n- 4 endpoints to call:\n  - POST /api/ai/compliance: returns brand_alignment, disclaimers, pricing_cross_check, recommended_action, retrieved_docs\n  - POST /api/ai/brief: returns campaign_goal, target_audience, expected_roi, risk_flags, ai_recommendation, retrieved_docs\n  - POST /api/ai/route-revision: returns change_type, suggested_owner, one_line_summary, urgency\n  - POST /api/ai/cascade: returns localized_variants, activation_schedule\n\nSTEP 1: Navigate and explore the existing frontend\ncd /Users/mernasalama/Desktop/Test\\ 1/MGT_449_GEN_AI/milestone_02_Github\nls gui/\n\nRead these files to understand the existing structure:\n- gui/app/page.tsx (main page)\n- gui/compo"}
